    "coverLine": "Generated by WorldEye Fraud Radar from public records and the author's pinned research. This report is a research document, not a finding of wrongdoing.",
    "researchLeadsDisclaimer": "Research leads in this report are statistical or record-matching observations from published public data. A research lead is a reason to look closer; it is not a finding of wrongdoing, and most entities above any statistical band have ordinary explanations (case mix, specialty practice patterns, contract type, reporting practices). Determinations of fraud are made by agencies and courts, not by this platform.",
    "noDesignationLine": "This report has not been reviewed by an attorney or other professional on behalf of the platform.",
    "whipBlock": "Report suspected fraud through the official channels — the federal fraud-reporting portal at america.gov/fraud (fraud.gov), the DOJ Fraud Whistleblower Incentive Program page at justice.gov/fraud/whistleblower, and for health-care programs the HHS-OIG hotline (linked from oig.hhs.gov). Fraud Radar prepares and organises research; tips must go through the official portal, and DOJ may deny an award for a tip that did not.\n\nDOJ's published framework is a reward of $10,000–$30,000 per distinct tip, paid after charges are unsealed, at DOJ's sole discretion. An announced 1% commission appears nowhere in DOJ's published programme materials and is not a programme term.\n\nFraud Radar never submits anything to any authority on a user's behalf, and never states that a user will receive an award. Eligibility and any award are DOJ's determination.",
    "whipTemplates": [
      "B",
      "G",
      "H"
    ],
    "evidenceExportWarning": "Exports leave the evidence vault's access control. Before sharing an export, check what you have included: the platform stores and indexes evidence, and you are responsible for the contents of files you choose to export.",
